---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Services — Jorge Benavides Aspiazu"
			description="IoT architecture reviews, embedded firmware development, production debugging, and system integration. Based in Lima, Peru."
		/>
		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
				max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
				margin: auto;
				padding: 3em 1em;
			}
			h1 {
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
			}
			.intro {
				margin-bottom: 2.5em;
				font-size: 1.05em;
				line-height: 1.7;
			}
			.service {
				margin-bottom: 2.5em;
			}
			.service h3 {
				margin-bottom: 0.25em;
				font-size: 1.3em;
			}
			.service .scope {
				color: rgb(var(--gray));
				font-size: 0.9em;
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
			}
			.portfolio {
				margin-top: 3em;
				padding-top: 2em;
				border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
			}
			.portfolio h2 {
				font-size: 1.6em;
				margin-bottom: 1em;
			}
			.portfolio-item {
				margin-bottom: 1.5em;
			}
			.portfolio-item strong {
				display: block;
				margin-bottom: 0.25em;
			}
			.cta {
				margin-top: 3em;
				padding: 2em;
				background: rgba(var(--gray-light), 50%);
				border-radius: 12px;
				text-align: center;
			}
			.cta h2 {
				font-size: 1.5em;
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
			}
			.cta a {
				display: inline-block;
				margin-top: 1em;
				padding: 0.75em 2em;
				background: var(--accent);
				color: white;
				text-decoration: none;
				border-radius: 8px;
				font-weight: 700;
				font-size: 1.05em;
			}
			.cta a:hover {
				background: var(--accent-dark);
				color: white;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Services</h1>

			<div class="intro">
				<p>
					I work with teams on existing IoT and connected systems — the kind where
					devices are already deployed, data is already flowing, and the problems are
					specific to your architecture.
				</p>
				<p>
					Most engagements start as focused technical work and expand as complexity
					surfaces. I operate across the full stack: PCB-level constraints through
					cloud infrastructure.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="service">
				<h3>Architecture Review</h3>
				<p class="scope">Project-based</p>
				<p>
					Deep review of your IoT or embedded system architecture. I look at device
					firmware structure, network topology, data ingestion pipelines, and the
					boundaries where components interact. You get a written report with
					specific recommendations — not a deck of generalities.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="service">
				<h3>IoT System Integration</h3>
				<p class="scope">Project-based</p>
				<p>
					Multi-network device deployments, protocol bridging (MQTT, CoAP, LoRaWAN,
					LTE-M), cloud ingestion pipelines, and device lifecycle management.
					Particularly experienced with heterogeneous fleets where no two device
					types behave the same.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="service">
				<h3>Production Debugging & Optimization</h3>
				<p class="scope">Retainer or project-based</p>
				<p>
					When something is broken in production and nobody can figure out why.
					Field-deployed devices dropping data, ingestion pipelines silently losing
					events, firmware crashes that only happen under load. I find the root cause
					and fix it.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="service">
				<h3>Embedded Firmware Development</h3>
				<p class="scope">Project-based</p>
				<p>
					Custom firmware for STM32, ESP32, and similar MCUs. Sensor integration,
					communication stacks, power management, OTA update systems. I write
					firmware that survives deployment — not just firmware that compiles.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="service">
				<h3>AI Intelligence Layer Design</h3>
				<p class="scope">Project-based</p>
				<p>
					Your IoT pipeline collects and stores data correctly. What it can't do is
					answer questions that weren't anticipated when it was designed. I design
					the intelligence layer that sits above your existing stack — defining the
					translation interface, scoping what the model can access, and connecting
					data sources the pipeline can't combine on its own.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="portfolio">
				<h2>Selected Work</h2>

				<div class="portfolio-item">
					<strong>0G Peru — IoT Network Operator</strong>
					<p>
						Turnkey IoT connectivity for industrial and utility clients in Peru.
						Full vertical: device provisioning, multi-network management (LoRaWAN,
						LTE-M, satellite), cloud data platform, and customer dashboards.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="portfolio-item">
					<strong>DataFlowLabs — Hardware + Cloud Platform</strong>
					<p>
						Hardware product line (DataEdge) and cloud platform (DataOS) for
						industrial monitoring. PCB design through Kubernetes deployment.
						Real-time data ingestion from heterogeneous sensor fleets.
					</p>
				</div>

			</div>

			<div class="cta">
				<h2>Let's talk about your system</h2>
				<p>
					Describe the problem you're facing. I'll tell you if I can help and
					how I'd approach it.
				</p>
				<a href="mailto:me@jobenas.com">me@jobenas.com</a>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
